The survey by Kong et al. in [38] analyzes both digital deepfakes and physical face presentation attacks (such as masks and printouts). Its emphasis is on biometrics and facial presentation verification rather than the structural composition of revisited environments. In contrast, ReScene is a dataset where the emphasis is on the inconsistency of scene-level and object-level information in revisit-based videos, and manipulations like insertion, deletion, and substitution of objects can be performed.

